	# Ticket 14 — Define Meta-Discovery using ordinary Discovery
	
	Priority: P0
	
	Depends on: Tickets 12 and 13
	
	## Context
	
	Discovery should be able to help improve Discovery itself without gaining a
	special self-analysis responsibility.
	
	The clean model is:
	
	```text
	Discovery on consumer resources
	→ consumer findings
	
	Discovery on Discovery field evaluations
	→ Discovery improvement findings
	```
	
	Both are ordinary Discovery runs.
	
	## Goal
	
	Document and test the generic Meta-Discovery workflow while keeping the engine
	completely unaware that the analyzed subject is Discovery itself.
	
	## Core rule
	
	There must be no:
	
	```text
	self_analysis mode
	meta mode
	discovery consumer adapter
	```
	
	From Discovery's point of view, field evaluations are simply another authorized
	corpus.
	
	## Workflow
	
	```text
	arbitrary consumer
	        ↓
	ordinary Discovery run
	        ↓
	human finding review
	        ↓
